## Financial Analysis

### Current State

Halden generates approximately **$27.9M in LTM revenue** (as of June 2025) with LTM EBITDA of approximately **$6.78M (~25% margin)** [14]. However, beneath these headline figures lies a deeply concerning trend: the company is experiencing sustained margin compression with revenues declining far faster than costs can adjust.

#### Revenue and Margin Erosion

| Metric | Trend | Monthly Slope | p-value | Significance |
|--------|-------|---------------|---------|---------------|
| Total Revenue | ↓ Declining | –$64,300/month | 0.0004 | Highly significant |
| Total COGS | → Flat | –$9,470/month | 0.164 | Not significant |
| Gross Profit | ↓ Declining | –$54,900/month | <0.00001 | Highly significant |
| EBITDA | ↓ Declining | –$49,800/month | <0.00001 | Highly significant |

